1
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:15,950
Bolivians, a propitious fate

2
00:00:16,011 --> 00:00:20,885
has at long last crowned
our vows and longings;

3
00:00:20,939 --> 00:00:25,768
This land is free, free at last.

4
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:29,471
Its servile state has now finally ceased.

5
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:35,500
The martial turmoil of yesterday,

6
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:40,308
and the horrible clamor of war,

7
00:00:40,542 --> 00:00:44,823
are followed today,
in harmonious contrast,

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,800
by sweet hymns of peace and unity.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,788
Are followed today,
in harmonious contrast,

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,536
by sweet hymns of peace and unity.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,757
Let us keep the lofty name
of our Fatherland

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,789
in glorious splendor.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,611
And, on its altars,
once more we must swear:

14
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:18,504
to die before we would live as slaves!

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,519
To die before we would live as slaves!

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,500
To die before we would live as slaves!